# The lines the Slang twin of default/main.frag may declare differently from the GLSL (task 0072, stage f), read by
# SlangPermutations in components-tests: "[<define set>] glsl-only: <line>"; every listed line must occur, so a stale
# entry fails the test. All of them are declarations the GLSL keeps and never reads (glslang keeps them, slangc drops
# them); a pipeline layout may hold bindings and a vertex stage may write outputs a shader does not read, so nothing
# the pipeline builds changes. Specialization constants that nothing reads (the UV set constants of maps a set does not
# have, `specular`) need no line: the checker does not list them (vsgUtil::readSpirvInterface).
#
# Without a map that reads the texture coordinates: the texCoord input (the last location).
# With per-pixel lighting (NORMAL with PBR, or with a normal or specular map): pointLightDiffuse (location 3 to 6,
#   after the members the set has), the vertex stage's point light sum, which the per-pixel lighting replaces.
# PARTICLE without NORMAL: the environment array (binding 1), the shadow map and its sampler (6, 7) and the object
#   uniform (set 1), which only the lit branches read, and with CLOUD_SHADOW the clouds' header buffer and shadow map
#   (13, 16), which only shadow() reads; pointLightDiffuse (2, or 3 after softParticleSize). The colour input (0) is
#   NOT an exception since toddhow's decision of 2026-11-04: the twin reads the particle's colour and alpha, which the
#   GLSL declares and never reads (lib/material/terms.slang; the one deliberate difference in the output).
